# Copy to .env at the repo root (Expo's CLI auto-loads .env for any
# EXPO_PUBLIC_* var since SDK 49 — no dotenv package involved, see
# node_modules/@expo/env). This is the *client* config; the auth API's own
# secrets (DB_*, JWT_SECRET, ...) are a separate file, server/.env.example
# — the two are never merged because server-only secrets must not end up
# inlined into a client bundle.

# Base URL the app's fetch client (src/lib/api/auth.ts) talks to. Unset, it
# defaults to http://localhost:3001 — fine for `npm run server` locally next
# to `docker compose up` from repo root, wrong for anything else:
#   - Simulator/emulator/device on the same LAN as a docker-compose host:
#       http://<host-lan-ip>:3001   (localhost inside the container/host
#       network is not reachable from a phone or a separate emulator VM)
#   - A real deploy behind TLS termination (server/README.md "What a real
#     deploy needs" #5 — not yet built):
#       https://api.yourdomain.example
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3001
